  era: "Section 16 \xB7 Mughal Empire \xB7 1526 \u2013 1857"
  title: Shah Jahan
  text: 'Shah Jahan, who ruled from 1628 to 1658, presided over the empire''s grandest building: the Taj Mahal, the Red Fort and the Jama Masjid of Delhi, and the Peacock Throne. He was deposed by his son Aurangzeb and died a captive in Agra.'
